<section data-analytics-location="approach" class="section journey-section" aria-labelledby="about-delivery-title">
  <div class="wrap about-story">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">FROM THE IDEA TO THE DELIVERY</p><h2 id="about-delivery-title" data-interest="about_delivery">Connecting architecture<br /><em>to delivery.</em></h2></div>
    <div class="about-prose">
      <p>I enjoy working where business goals and engineering decisions meet. I start by understanding what needs to be delivered and when, then look at the team's current tools, frustrations, and slowdowns.</p>
      <p>That's where ideas take shape: a clearer deployment process, a better feedback loop, or a platform capability that removes a recurring obstacle. I like taking those ideas through to a working solution people can use.</p>
      <div class="about-example">
        <p class="eyebrow">IN PRACTICE / EARLIER FEEDBACK</p>
        <p>In one recent project, I worked with a frontend team to create <strong>preview environments for individual pull requests</strong>. Developers could share a live version of a feature before merging it, and the preview stayed up to date as their work changed. The frontend team added a simple way for reviewers to choose which version to explore.</p>
        <p>Business stakeholders gained earlier access, developers received quicker feedback, and QA could focus on features that had already met the business's expectations. It's a good example of what I want infrastructure to accomplish: give people more autonomy and help them work together.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section data-analytics-location="approach" class="section wrap about-story" aria-labelledby="about-tooling-title">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">DESIGNED FOR THE PEOPLE USING IT</p><h2 id="about-tooling-title" data-interest="about_tooling">Developer tooling<br /><em>is a product.</em></h2></div>
  <div class="about-prose">
    <p>I build systems for developers with the same mindset I bring to building an application. The workflow should be understandable, useful, and shaped around the people using it.</p>
    <p>I usually start with a demo, put the system in the hands of a few experienced users, and refine it with their feedback before introducing it to the wider team. Making a tool work well for its users is part of the engineering.</p>
    <p>My experience spans GPU infrastructure, distributed platforms, and Kubernetes deployments in environments without internet access. Those projects have given me different ways to approach a problem—and an appreciation for choosing an approach the team can realistically operate.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section data-analytics-location="approach" class="section journey-section" aria-labelledby="about-studio-title">
